course: dictionary
lesson: 4129
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them, the context, tell you which meaning the writer wants. Take the word glider. «A glider has no engine; it is towed up and then floats on rising warm air.» Here the clues are no engine, towed and floats, so a glider must be a light aircraft that flies without a motor.
explain: The same word can point to a creature. «Sugar gliders are tiny marsupials with skin flaps between their legs that can glide about fifty metres from tree to tree at night.» Tree to tree and skin flaps tell you a sugar glider is an animal, not a machine.
explain: Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then try it in the sentence instead of the hard word. If you say «The garden glider was comfy» and it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. If it does not, try another meaning.
fact: A glider is a light aircraft with long wings and no engine. It flies by riding on air currents.
fact: A glider can also be any thing or animal that glides, like a paper glider or a sugar glider.
fact: A sugar glider is a tiny marsupial, or a small flying possum, that glides from tree to tree.
fact: In the UK, a glider is a garden swing seat that moves smoothly back and forth. In the US, it is called a glider chair.
fact: Context clues, like «no engine» or «tree to tree», tell you which meaning of glider the writer means.
exercise: «A glider has no engine; it is towed up and then floats on rising warm air.» What is a glider in this sentence? | A small flying possum | A garden swing seat | *A light aircraft with long wings and no engine
exercise: «Sugar gliders are tiny marsupials with skin flaps between their legs that can glide about fifty metres from tree to tree at night.» What is a sugar glider here? | A swing for the garden | A kind of aeroplane | *A tiny marsupial that glides from tree to tree | A paper plane
exercise: In a science lesson, a pupil tests a «paper glider». What is the glider in this phrase? | A seat in the garden | A large engine | *Something made of paper that glides through the air | A type of tree
test: «Go into the dark nocturnal room and your eyes slowly find a sugar glider sailing from branch to branch on flaps of skin.» Which clue shows that a sugar glider is an animal? | *Flaps of skin and branch to branch | Dark room | Your eyes slowly find it | Nocturnal room
test: «Gliders can stay up for hours and fly hundreds of kilometres.» Which clue shows that a glider is an aircraft? | Hours | Stay up | Gliders | *Fly hundreds of kilometres
exam: The word glider has three meanings. Which one is a garden swing seat that moves smoothly back and forth? | A kind of wing | A small flying possum | A light aircraft with no engine | *A garden swing seat
